    "body": "STR:\r\nI entered `802.11` in the Focus (7.0) address bar, trying to search for the [Wikipedia page about IEEE 802.11](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IEEE_802.11). Focus interrupted `802.11` as an address (IP or domain name, I don't know).\r\n\r\nACTUAL RESULT:\r\nFocus shows an error page with mojibake characters: `The URL canâ€™t be shown`.\r\n\r\nEXPECTED RESULT:\r\nIn Firefox for iOS, entering `802.11` loads a WebKit error page showing `The URL can’t be shown`. Or the browser could just treat invalid addresses as search terms, which might find a link to an appropriate page. However, some users might consider it a privacy violation.",
